BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-reflection-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T152941Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Reflection (All Disciplines)
DESCRIPTION:Reflection is a Pro Helvetia grant supporting collective mediat
 ion projects that use innovative formats to foster critical reflection on 
 artistic practice and cultural transformation\, across all supported disci
 plines (design\, literature\, music\, performing arts\, visual arts\, and 
 innovation and society). Open to collectives comprising at least two cultu
 ral practitioners (artists\, creatives\, cultural practitioners\, or art e
 ducators)\; solo projects are excluded. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection
  to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular a
 rtistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swi
 ss connection. For international collaborations\, at least 50 percent of p
 ractitioners must be from Switzerland. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 25\,000\, and n
 o more than 50 percent of the total budget. Deadlines twice a year: 1 Marc
 h (23:59 CET) and 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia por
 tal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Collect
 ives of at least two cultural practitioners\; for international collaborat
 ions at least 50 percent must be from Switzerland.\nAward: Maximum CHF 25\
 ,000 (cannot exceed 50 percent of total budget). No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Collective mediation project fostering critical reflection\; deadlin
 es twice yearly (1 March and 1 September).\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch
 /en/find-support/reflection?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/reflection?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Collectives of at least two cultural practitioners\; for internati
 onal collaborations at least 50 percent must be from Switzerland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260824T152941Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foodculture-days-kitchen-central-location-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260824T152941Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Kitchen / Central Location Open Call (foodculture day
 s Biennale\, Vevey 2027)
DESCRIPTION:foodculture days is opening up The Kitchen / Central Location\,
  the living heart of its biennale in Vevey\, to an outside collective for 
 the festival's 6th edition. The Kitchen is at once an open-air kitchen\, a
  gathering space and an artistic installation\, sited by the lake on the E
 splanade de la Paix along a busy promenade\, hosting multidisciplinary pro
 jects\, concerts\, themed meals\, public discussions\, citizens' assemblie
 s and moments of collective cooking. The call asks for new ways of inhabit
 ing it. WHO THEY WANT: a transdisciplinary collective of scientists\, arti
 sts\, designers\, craftspeople\, cooks\, activists and architects\, either
  newly formed or already active\; collaboration across generations\, cultu
 res and levels of expertise is encouraged. WHAT IS OFFERED: an open-air ci
 tizen experimentation laboratory in Vevey's public space\, framed around r
 ethinking ways of living and the relationship to time and to creation\, an
 d thinking together about the conditions under which multidisciplinary pra
 ctices can flourish. THE BRIEF: kitchen and hospitality\, lunch and dinner
  service\, vegetarian meals with a vegan option. Meals should be affordabl
 e\, seasonal where fresh produce is involved\, and conceived in the spirit
  of a communal canteen: simple\, generous\, nourishing and full of flavour
 . Expected covers are roughly 100 guests Wednesday to Thursday and roughly
  150 Friday to Sunday. WHAT THE FESTIVAL PROVIDES: curatorial support to d
 evelop the proposal\, with particular attention to the themed meals\; intr
 oductions to local producers\, growers and artisans including farm visits 
 and foraging sites\; production support and volunteers throughout\; and st
 andard professional kitchen equipment and cooking facilities. BUDGET: CHF 
 15\,000 all-inclusive (VAT included) covering travel\, visas\, equipment r
 ental\, any additional kitchen equipment\, per diems\, materials and artis
 t fees\; food costs and accommodation in Vevey are covered separately. THE
  SPACE: the pavilion\, called Cuisine\, is a modular metal structure assem
 bled from repurposed agricultural greenhouse components on a 3.1 metre bid
 irectional grid\, with pillars and arches forming ridge vaults\, a textile
  covering naturally dyed yellow with reseda\, and a terracotta brick heart
 h for wood-fired cooking laid directly on the floor. It comes with dining 
 tables\, low tables\, a reception table\, a shelf\, a bar\, pendant lights
 \, 30 cushions\, removable curtains\, flags\, blackboards and signage pane
 ls\, and can expand\, contract or be reconfigured. TIMELINE: Phase 1 deadl
 ine 31 August 2026 at midnight CET\; three shortlisted proposals selected 
 in late September\, each invited to an online meeting and paid a CHF 250 r
 esearch fee for Phase 2\; final project selected and announced in early Oc
 tober 2026\; collaborative development with the foodculture days architect
 ural team October to November\; production December to February\; build an
 d installation in Vevey 1 to 16 June 2027\, with the collective present th
 roughout those two weeks\; 6th edition of the biennale 16 to 20 June 2027.
  PHASE 1 QUESTIONS: tell us about your collective (origins\, intention\, w
 hat makes you special)\; member biographies with collective or individual 
 portfolios\, website\, Instagram\, city of residence and practices\; what 
 the concept consists of in terms of food and cuisine\, relationships\, and
  scenography and spatial research\; what you want to put into practice in 
 the central pavilion\, your vision and the kind of experience you want to 
 create\; any special requirements\; and references\, including a quote rep
 resenting the collective\, two reference texts\, three images and optional
 ly video. An Open Call Information Kit\, a recording of the online informa
 tion session and a Q&A are published on the open call site and are worth r
 eading before applying.\n\nOrganisation: foodculture days\nLocation: Vevey
 \, Switzerland. The Kitchen is built on the Esplanade de la Paix by the la
 keside. The selected collective must be present in Vevey for the two-week 
 build and installation\, 1 to 16 June 2027\, and through the biennale 16 t
 o 20 June 2027.\nAward: CHF 15\,000 all-inclusive project budget (VAT incl
 uded)\, covering travel\, visas\, equipment and additional kitchen equipme
 nt rental\, per diems\, materials and artist fees. Food costs and accommod
 ation in Vevey are covered separately by foodculture days. Three shortlist
 ed collectives each receive a CHF 250 research fee to develop their propos
 al in Phase 2. One collective is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 October 2026 to June 2027: collaborative development October-November\, pr
 oduction December-February\, on-site build 1-16 June 2027\, biennale 16-20
  June 2027\n\nMore: https://opencall.foodculturedays.com/en?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencall.foodculturedays.com/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Vevey\, Switzerland. The Kitchen is built on the Esplanade de la P
 aix by the lakeside. The selected collective must be present in Vevey for 
 the two-week build and installation\, 1 to 16 June 2027\, and through the 
 biennale 16 to 20 June 2027.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
